WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.567
t-SNE.

2
00:00:01.867 --> 00:00:04.576
A projection that reveals clusters beautifully.

3
00:00:04.576 --> 00:00:07.400
Interviewers love asking what it cannot tell you.

4
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:12.133
t-SNE is a non-linear projection built for one job.

5
00:00:12.433 --> 00:00:16.333
It preserves local neighborhoods, so points that were close stay close.

6
00:00:16.633 --> 00:00:19.467
That makes it great at revealing cluster structure.

7
00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:21.967
Here is the recipe.

8
00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:25.933
Start with distances in the original high dimensional space.

9
00:00:26.233 --> 00:00:28.500
Convert them into neighbor probabilities.

10
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.800
Arrange points in 2D so those neighbor relationships are matched.

11
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.900
Groups come out as crisp islands.

12
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.867
How does it differ from PCA?

13
00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:40.614
PCA can only rotate and project.

14
00:00:40.614 --> 00:00:43.367
t-SNE can untangle curved structure.

15
00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:48.433
Where PCA smears a curved shape flat, t-SNE pulls it apart into islands.

16
00:00:48.733 --> 00:00:51.100
t-SNE separates what PCA smears.

17
00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:53.333
Here is the code.

18
00:00:53.633 --> 00:00:57.733
We load the digits dataset, which has sixty four dimensions per image.

19
00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:00.117
Then we project to two dimensions.

20
00:01:00.117 --> 00:01:01.833
Perplexity is the main knob.

21
00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:04.333
Now the warning label.

22
00:01:04.633 --> 00:01:09.068
Distances between clusters mean nothing, and neither do cluster sizes.

23
00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:14.516
The algorithm stretches dense regions, and different perplexity values redraw the map.

24
00:01:14.516 --> 00:01:17.367
Read it only as: these points group together.

25
00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:20.000
Here is how it pays off.

26
00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:23.433
PCA showed your light curve features as one smear.

27
00:01:23.733 --> 00:01:28.500
t-SNE splits it into islands, and one is almost entirely false positives.

28
00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.896
That discovery becomes a new feature.

29
00:01:30.896 --> 00:01:35.200
And if a teammate measures the gap between islands, you deliver the warning.

30
00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:37.131
Let's recap.

31
00:01:37.131 --> 00:01:40.667
t-SNE is a non-linear projection that keeps neighborhoods.

32
00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:43.433
It reveals islands that PCA smears.

33
00:01:43.733 --> 00:01:46.967
But distances and sizes between clusters mean nothing.

34
00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:48.633
Next up: UMAP.
